# Line endings.
#
# These files are read by a Linux shell, and a shell will not run a script
# whose lines end in CRLF - it fails with "bad interpreter: no such file or
# directory", which names the interpreter and not the real problem. This
# repository is edited on Windows, where git's default is to store what the
# working copy has, so without this a routine edit could commit a build
# script that only fails on the machine it exists for.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.desktop   text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to translate anything inside them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.apk binary
*.exe binary
*.vsix binary
